{"docId": "doc-dff4b9df26", "engine": "docling", "doclingVersion": "2.132.0", "title": "sample-harmonic-upload", "pages": [{"page": 1, "width": 612.0, "height": 792.0}, {"page": 2, "width": 612.0, "height": 792.0}], "items": [{"id": "p1-i0", "kind": "section_header", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.31955, "y": 0.15156, "w": 0.36091, "h": 0.04941}, "text": "Harmonic Distortion Notes: The Two-Parameter Sine Model"}, {"id": "p1-i1", "kind": "text", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.4419, "y": 0.22142, "w": 0.12311, "h": 0.01652}, "text": "A. Researcher \u2217"}, {"id": "p1-i2", "kind": "text", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.44393, "y": 0.25372, "w": 0.11215, "h": 0.01509}, "text": "October 2026"}, {"id": "p1-i3", "kind": "section_header", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.46419, "y": 0.32169, "w": 0.07163, "h": 0.01258}, "text": "Abstract"}, {"id": "p1-i4", "kind": "text", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.17398, "y": 0.34559, "w": 0.65205, "h": 0.05786}, "text": "We study the simplest two-parameter oscillation and ask how its amplitude and frequency controls interact when a signal is sampled at fixed intervals. Throughout the note the amplitude is written a and the angular frequency is written b; the independent variable is time, written x."}, {"id": "p1-i5", "kind": "section_header", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.12941, "y": 0.42984, "w": 0.16036, "h": 0.01811}, "text": "1 The model"}, {"id": "p1-i6", "kind": "text", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.12941, "y": 0.4641, "w": 0.50902, "h": 0.01377}, "text": "The signal of interest is the pure sine with modulated amplitude:"}, {"id": "p1-i7", "kind": "formula", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.44796, "y": 0.49504, "w": 0.42263, "h": 0.01377}, "latex": "y = a \\sin ( b x ) ."}, {"id": "p1-i8", "kind": "text", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.12941, "y": 0.52599, "w": 0.74117, "h": 0.04799}, "text": "Here a controls the peak value of the signal and b controls how fast the oscillation repeats. Doubling a stretches the curve vertically; doubling b compresses it horizontally by one half. When a is negative the curve flips."}, {"id": "p1-i9", "kind": "section_header", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.12941, "y": 0.60013, "w": 0.38221, "h": 0.01811}, "text": "2 Envelope of a damped variant"}, {"id": "p1-i10", "kind": "text", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.12941, "y": 0.63439, "w": 0.45569, "h": 0.01377}, "text": "For comparison, the damped variant decays exponentially:"}, {"id": "p1-i11", "kind": "formula", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.42852, "y": 0.66387, "w": 0.44207, "h": 0.01523}, "latex": "u ( t ) = e ^ { - t } \\cos ( \\omega t ) ."}, {"id": "p1-i12", "kind": "text", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.12941, "y": 0.69627, "w": 0.74116, "h": 0.03088}, "text": "Both formulas are studied numerically in the accompanying worksheet; the sweep below fixes the sampling grid and varies the two parameters of (1)."}, {"id": "p1-i13", "kind": "section_header", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.12941, "y": 0.7533, "w": 0.22565, "h": 0.01811}, "text": "3 A sampled trace"}, {"id": "p1-i14", "kind": "text", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.12941, "y": 0.78756, "w": 0.58218, "h": 0.01377}, "text": "A short sample of the model with a = 1.5 and b = 2 is plotted in Figure 1."}, {"id": "p1-i15", "kind": "footnote", "page": 1, "bbox": {"x": 0.149, "y": 0.8891, "w": 0.24055, "h": 0.01309}, "text": "\u2217 Preliminary draft; worked example."}, {"id": "p2-i16", "kind": "figure", "page": 2, "bbox": {"x": 0.28306, "y": 0.39514, "w": 0.43718, "h": 0.17409}}, {"id": "p2-i17", "kind": "caption", "page": 2, "bbox": {"x": 0.26547, "y": 0.59737, "w": 0.46906, "h": 0.01377}, "text": "Figure 1: One period-sampled trace of (1) at a = 1.5, b = 2."}]}